    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Nothing below is a rule about music. Every `assert` here is a claim a" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// composer chose to write down about one passage, and the compiler either" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// proves it or says exactly which note refuses. Delete an assertion and the" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// piece is unchanged: an assertion adds no note, no time, and no barline, and" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// the only trace it leaves is one line of provenance under the notes it" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// covers." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// The claims are a fixed family, not an extension point. There are five, they" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// are checked after the passage has been instantiated in its real context," },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and nothing here becomes a global style rule because it happens to be" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// checkable locally — a piece may leave a scale on the next system and no" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// warning follows it out." },
